description:
Design a Fibonacci sequence generator that computes and outputs an 8-bit Fibonacci number on each 12th clock cycle. Upon receiving a reset signal, the module initializes the first two Fibonacci numbers to 1. On each clock pulse, it updates the sequence by calculating the next Fibonacci number and maintaining a count of clock cycles to control the output rate. The generated Fibonacci number is available at the output after every 12 clock cycles, allowing for a steady progression through the Fibonacci sequence.
module top_module(
    input clk,
    input reset,
    output reg [7:0] out
);

code:
module top_module(
    input clk,
    input reset,
    output reg [7:0] out
);reg [7:0] a, b, c;
reg [3:0] cnt;

always @(posedge clk) begin
    if (reset) begin
        a <= 8'h01;
        b <= 8'h01;
        c <= 8'h00;
        cnt <= 4'h0;
    end else begin
        c <= a + b;
        a <= b;
        b <= c;
        if (cnt == 4'hB) begin
            out <= c;
            cnt <= 4'h0;
        end else begin
            cnt <= cnt + 1;
        end
    end
end

endmodule

