Design a one-hot state machine with four distinct states. The state machine transitions between states on the rising edge of the clock signal, starting from state 's1' when the reset signal is activated. Upon each clock pulse, the state will progress sequentially through 's1', 's2', 's3', and 's4', eventually looping back to 's1', ensuring that only one state is active at any given time, indicated by the respective one-hot encoded output signal.
