description:
Design a circuit that generates a pulse output based on a programmable timing interval. The module counts clock pulses using a 29-bit counter, and when the count reaches a specified threshold (defined by parameter N), it resets. The output pulse remains HIGH for a specified duration (defined by the parameter pulse) before transitioning to LOW. This functionality can be used in applications requiring a precise time-controlled pulse, such as clock division or timing signal generation.
module top_module(
    input clk,
    output reg pulse_output
    );

code:
module top_module(
    input clk,
    output reg pulse_output
    );reg[28:0] cnt;
    parameter N = 10;
    parameter pulse = 1;

    always @(posedge clk) begin 
        if(cnt < N-1)
            cnt <= cnt + 1;
        else cnt <= 0;
    end

    always @(posedge clk) begin
        if(cnt < pulse)
            pulse_output <= 1;
        else pulse_output <= 0;
    end
endmodule

