Design a BCD (Binary-Coded Decimal) converter that translates a 4-bit binary input into an 8-bit output representing its BCD equivalent. The module maps binary values from 0 to 9 to specific BCD representations in the output, where each BCD digit is indicated by a unique 1-bit active signal within the 8-bit output. For inputs outside of the binary 0-9 range, the output defaults to zero.
