description:
Design a circuit that controls a 4-bit LED output based on two input switches, sw0 and sw1. The module implements various logic operations: LED[0] represents the logical AND of sw0 and sw1; LED[1] is a buffered version of sw0 conditional on sw1; LED[2] outputs the result of a NAND operation followed by a double negation, effectively creating an AND function; meanwhile, LED[3] also reflects the AND of sw0 and sw1. Overall, this module serves to demonstrate the combination of different logic gates and signal conditioning involving the provided switches.
