description:
Design a 3-to-8 decoder with a two-stage pipeline. The module accepts a 3-bit input `select` and generates an 8-bit output `out` where only one bit corresponds to the binary representation of the `select` input, indicating which output is active. The design includes two registers, `pipeline1` and `pipeline2`, to store intermediate states, providing a level of timing and synchronization. The output `out` is continuously updated on the positive edge of the clock based on the value stored in `pipeline1`, ensuring that the decoded output is stable and correctly synchronized with the clock signal.
module top_module(
    input clk,
    input [2:0] select,
    output reg [7:0] out
);

code:
module top_module(
    input clk,
    input [2:0] select,
    output reg [7:0] out
);reg [7:0] pipeline1, pipeline2;

always @(posedge clk) begin
    pipeline1 <= pipeline2;
    pipeline2 <= {~select[2], ~select[1], ~select[0], ~select[2], ~select[1], select[0], ~select[2], select[1], ~select[0]};
end

assign out = pipeline1;

endmodule

