description:
Design a D flip-flop with asynchronous reset and clock-enable functionality. When the reset signal is asserted, the output Q is set to LOW. On each rising edge of the clock, if the clock enable (ce) is active, the output Q is updated to the value of the input D, allowing for controlled data storage based on the clock and enable signals.
module top_module(
    input D,Clk,reset,ce,
    output reg Q
    );

code:
module top_module(
    input D,Clk,reset,ce,
    output reg Q
    );always @(posedge Clk)
    if (reset)
    begin
        Q <= 1'b0;
    end else if (ce)
    begin
        Q <= D;
    end
endmodule

