Design a clock divider circuit that generates a lower frequency output signal from an input clock. The module uses a 28-bit counter to track the number of input clock cycles. It resets the counter after reaching a predefined divisor value. The output clock signal toggles based on the counter value, producing a square wave with a frequency that is half of the input clock frequency when the counter value reaches the specified threshold. This setup is useful for reducing clock speeds in digital systems or generating specific timing signals.
