Design a module that calculates the sum of specific processed inputs. It includes an "any edge" detection mechanism where it computes the output by performing a bitwise AND operation between the input and its left-shifted version, effectively identifying 'any edge' transitions. It also separates a 16-bit input into upper and lower 8-bit segments. Finally, it computes the sum of the results from the "any edge" output and both segments of the split input, yielding an 8-bit output representing the combined result.
module top_module(
    input [7:0] anyedge_in, // 8-bit input for the anyedge module
    input [15:0] split_in, // 16-bit input for the split module
    output reg [7:0] sum // 8-bit output for the sum of the two inputs
);

