description:
Create a 3-bit priority encoder for an 8-bit input. The module outputs the binary representation of the highest active input bit, with priority given to the leftmost bit. If the highest active bit is the first bit (bit 7), the output will be 4 (3'b100), for the second bit (bit 6) it will be 2 (3'b010), and for the third bit (bit 5) it will be 1 (3'b001). If no inputs are active, the output will be 0 (3'b000).
module top_module(
    input [7:0] code,
    output reg [2:0] out
);

