description:
Design a 9-bit wide adder that computes the sum of two 8-bit inputs, A and B, producing a 9-bit output S. The first bit of the output corresponds to the sum of the least significant bits of A and B, while subsequent bits are calculated in a loop to handle the carry generated from the addition of each bit, ensuring full propagation of carry bits across all eight bits. The sum includes an additional bit for overflow, accommodating scenarios where the sum exceeds the maximum representable value of 8 bits.
