description:
Design a parity generator and checker for an n-bit data input, where n is set to 8. The module computes the parity bit based on the specified parity type: even or odd. If the parity type is 0, it outputs a '1' if the number of set bits in the input data is odd (indicating an error in even parity), while for odd parity (when parityType is 1), it outputs a '1' if the number of set bits is even (indicating an error in odd parity). This functionality is essential for error detection in digital communication systems.
module top_module(
  input [n-1:0] data,
  input parityType,
  output reg p
);

code:
module top_module(
  input [n-1:0] data,
  input parityType,
  output reg p
);parameter n = 8; // number of data bits

integer i;
integer count;

always @(*) begin
  count = 0;
  for (i = 0; i < n; i = i + 1) begin
    count = count + data[i];
  end

  if (parityType == 1'b0) begin // even parity
    p = (count % 2 == 1) ? 1'b1 : 1'b0;
  end else begin // odd parity
    p = (count % 2 == 0) ? 1'b1 : 1'b0;
  end
end

endmodule

