description:
Develop a clock divider circuit that generates a lower frequency output clock (clk_out) from an input clock (clk). The output clock toggles its state after a specified count of 652 clock cycles, achieved by incrementing a 10-bit counter on each rising edge of the input clock. When the counter reaches this predefined threshold defined by the parameter 'count_to', the output clock is toggled to create a divided clock signal, effectively reducing the frequency of the input clock.
module top_module(
    input clk,
    output reg clk_out = 1'b0
    );

code:
module top_module(
    input clk,
    output reg clk_out = 1'b0
    );reg [9:0] counter = 10'b0; 
	 parameter count_to = 651; 


	always@(posedge clk)
	begin	
		if(counter == count_to) 
		begin
			counter <= 10'b0; 
			clk_out <= ~clk_out;
		end
		else
			counter <= counter + 1'b1; 
	end
endmodule

